constructed
route: GET /tasks/<pod>
status: 200
built-from: task-done.json, with a second task that is running
docket: docket 0.3.0b1 (API 6), source checkout 46e54ec7, read and not run
source: specs/api/operator-api.spec.md "Task answers" (the paragraphs on current and rev) and specs/data/serve-read-api.spec.md "Task cursor"
date: 2026-11-01
note: from the spec. Not captured, because the capture script queues no task that stays running, and the only answers it holds are of tasks refused at claim. The plain list: every task of the pod, each as GET /tasks/<pod>/<id> sends it, with rev; a running task carries current, and one started at the CLI has channel cli and no externalRef. Its keys are those of a captured task plus rev and current, which the spec lists; the values are made up.
